WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.200
Look at these two scratch cards. One's a

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:06.080
winner, and one's garbage. Yet, there's

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:07.800
a way to tell without scratching either

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:09.800
of them. It all started when a guy got

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:11.280
fired and spent five bucks on two

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:13.160
scratch cards on the way home. He

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:15.160
scratches one and wins his five bucks

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:17.360
back, but instead of celebrating like a

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:19.440
normal person, he gets suspicious. If

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:20.800
the lottery decides exactly how many

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:22.880
winners get printed, how does the

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:24.800
machine know which ones they are? So, he

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:26.760
does what any sane person would do. He

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:28.680
blows his entire severance check on a

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:30.520
huge stack, spreads them across his

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:32.400
apartment floor, and stares until

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:34.160
something jumps out. Every card has

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:35.800
little grids of numbers printed right on

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:38.120
the front, and most of the numbers show

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:39.920
up two or three times, but a few only

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:41.840
show up once. And whenever [music] three

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:43.840
of those loners line up in a row, it's a

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:45.520
winner, which means this guy just

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:47.520
cracked the lottery. He could walk into

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:49.600
every gas station in the state and clean

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:51.880
them out. So, what does he do? He calls

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:54.120
the lottery. "Sir, that's impossible."

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:55.720
Okay, so he walks into their office with

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:57.400
a box full of cards he's never

00:00:55.720 --> 00:01:00.000
scratched, [music] sorted into winners

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:01.840
and losers, and gets 90% of them right.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.040
By the end of the week, the game is gone

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:05.040
from every store.

